  "From the original disc": "",
  "No image needed.": "",
  "Put the disc in, press <kbd>START</kbd> for OPL's main menu and choose <strong>RA: check disc support</strong>, then <strong>RA: launch disc</strong>. The check reads the disc through the console's own drive and asks the PC the same way it does for an image. The launch boots the disc under OPL's in-game hooks, so telemetry and unlocks work as they do from USB.": "",
  "You give up OPL's virtual memory cards, per-game compatibility patches and cheats. They live in the part of OPL that emulates the drive, and a real disc does not use it.": "",
  "The same window for your emulator play.": "",
  "With the console off, xeRAbora follows your RetroAchievements account: the game you are in, the unlocks as they land, what to chase next, missable warnings, your library and the leaderboards. The difference is who unlocks.": "",
  "With the PS2 · the page turns gold": "",
  "With the PS2: the console streams memory to xeRAbora, which unlocks on RetroAchievements.": "",
